title: 'Decided: in a view whose every root is the user''s, a switch to the user''s overrides is refused; a switch back never is.'
pid: 857028c8-d9c0-4cea-960c-e903c87b2874
body: |2-
  There the two choices draw the same thing, so switching would only
  plant a mode-line mark that means nothing; the refusal says the view
  shows the user's overrides already. A view can come to have only owned
  roots while switched (editing a foreign root forks it and makes the
  clone the root), so the way back must stay open. A buffer of the diff
  view, which substitutes nothing, refuses both.
